m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Threonine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This network maps plausible abiotic formation pathways of threonine from simple C1 and C2 feedstocks, integrating hydrothermal and surface prebiotic environments, leveraging Strecker-like cyanohydrin and aminonitrile chemistry, aldol condensations, and subsequent hydrolysis and amination steps. Several pathways use cross-aldol chemistry, different keto acid precursors, hydrothermal reductive amination and surface-catalyzed transformations, providing pathway diversity.\n\nMOLECULES (16 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2 (hydrogen gas) [starting]\n  - mol_003: CH4 (methane) [starting]\n  - mol_004: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_005: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_006: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_007: CH3CHO (acetaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H6O2 (glyceraldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C2H3NO (glycinonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C3H5NO (serinol) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C4H7NO3 (threonine) [target]\n  - mol_012: C3H5NO2 (alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C2H4O2 (acetic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: C3H4O3 (pyruvic acid) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C4H5NO2 (2-amino-3-oxobutyric acid) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C2H2O2 (glycolaldehyde) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_007 (Acetaldehyde synthesis via reduction of CO2) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_001, mol_002 -> mol_006 (Formaldehyde synthesis from CO2 and H2) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_006 -> mol_016 (Glycolaldehyde formation via formose reaction) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_016, mol_006 -> mol_008 (Glyceraldehyde formation via glycolaldehyde aldol condensation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_008 -> mol_014 (Pyruvic acid synthesis via oxidation of glyceraldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_014, mol_004, mol_002 -> mol_012 (Alanine formation via reductive amination of pyruvic acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_007: mol_006, mol_007 -> mol_013 (Acetic acid synthesis from methanal/ethanal oxidation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_014, mol_004, mol_005 -> mol_015 (Pyruvic acid Strecker synthesis to aminonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_015, mol_008 -> mol_011 (Hydrolysis of aminonitrile to threonine) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_010: mol_008, mol_004 -> mol_010 (Serinol formation by amination of glyceraldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_011: mol_007, mol_009 -> mol_015 (Aldol condensation between acetaldehyde and glycine intermediates) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_016, mol_004, mol_005 -> mol_009 (Glycinonitrile synthesis (Strecker) from glycolaldehyde, ammonia, and HCN) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Formose-sugar aldehyde -> Strecker-aminonitrile -> Hydrolysis Pathway (6 steps)\n  - P2: Aldol-acetaldehyde plus glycinonitrile condensation route (4 steps)\n  - P3: Alanine extension pathway via two-carbon elongation (6 steps)\n  - P4: Serinol-based pathway (4 steps)\n  - P5: Acetic acid-Keto acid pathway (5 steps)\n  - P6: HCN-driven direct Strecker pathway (3 steps)\n  - P7: Secondary aldol pathway from glycolaldehyde and glyceraldehyde units (4 steps)\n  - P8: Direct amination of C3 backbone pathway (4 steps)\n  - P9: Chain-elongation via aminonitrile condensation (3 steps)\n  - P10: Formaldehyde-driven side pathway (5 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 12 reactions | 0 balanced as written | 0 balanceable with coefficients | 12 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: CO2 + H2 + CH4 -> CH3CHO | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; H2 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: CO2 + H2 -> CH2O | reactants minus products: O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: CH2O -> C2H2O2 | reactants minus products: C-1, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: C2H2O2 + CH2O -> C3H6O2 | reactants minus products: H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: C3H6O2 -> C3H4O3 | reactants minus products: H+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C3H4O3 + NH3 + H2 -> C3H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: CH2O + CH3CHO -> C2H4O2 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: C3H4O3 + NH3 + HCN -> C4H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_009 UNBALANCED: C4H5NO2 + C3H6O2 -> C4H7NO3 | reactants minus products: C+3, H+2, O+2 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: C3H6O2 + NH3 -> C3H5NO | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_011 UNBALANCED: CH3CHO + C2H3NO -> C4H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) 