ine aldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_011, mol_003 -> mol_010, H2O (Direct amination of serine to threonine (methyl transfer)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_013: mol_005, mol_007, mol_006 -> mol_011, H2O (Strecker synthesis of serine from glyceraldehyde and HCN/ammonia) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_015, mol_003 -> mol_016, H2O (Aldol condensation between glycinonitrile and acetaldehyde to give 2-aminoprop-2-enoic acid nitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_015: mol_016, H2O -> mol_013, NH3 (Hydrolysis of 2-oxopropanenitrile to 2-aminoprop-2-enoic acid (dehydroalanine)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_016: mol_013, mol_004 -> mol_008 (Addition of glycolaldehyde to dehydroalanine to yield threonine aldehyde) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Formose\u2013Aldol\u2013Strecker\u2013Hydrolysis route (5 steps)\n  - P2: Reductive amination\u2013Aldol\u2013Cyanation route (6 steps)\n  - P3: Aminoacetaldehyde\u2013Aldol route (5 steps)\n  - P4: Serine methylation pathway (4 steps)\n  - P5: Prebiotic glycinonitrile\u2013Aldol mechanism (4 steps)\n  - P6: Direct Strecker on threonine aldehyde followed by hydrolysis (5 steps)\n  - P7: Aldol\u2013serine\u2013methylation loop (2 steps)\n  - P8: Glycolaldehyde\u2013Ethanolamine\u2013aldol loop (5 steps)\n  - P9: Aminonitrile\u2013enone pathway (4 steps)\n  - P10: Serine via glyceraldehyde then methylation (4 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 16 reactions | 0 balanced as written | 1 balanceable with coefficients | 3 UNBALANCED | 12 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 balanceable: CH2O -> C2H4O2 + CH2O\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C2H4O2 + C2H4O -> C3H6O3 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_003 unchecked: H2O: unknown molecule ID\n  - rxn_004 unchecked